<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 57,555 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 57,555 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 57,555 tonnes of export and import cargo in 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Monday compared to 68,977 tonnes in the same period on Sunday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>				    Monday	March 9</p>
<p>    Export cargo		30,085	21,054</p>
<p>    Import cargo		27,470	47,923</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, five ships sailed and two berthed. In the next 24 hours, four are expected to sail and seven are expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at Karachi Port:</p>
<p>    Commodity	  Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		   Berthing</p>
<p>High speed diesel    75,000	 Chesa Peak City    11/3</p>
<p>Containers		  250	 Ibn Al-Haitham     13/3</p>
<p>Palm oil		 12,000	 Wawasen Courage    15/3</p>
<p>Vehicles		    107	 Arcadia Highway    16/3</p>
<p>Containers		  240	 Dammam Bay	   19/3</p>
<p>Phosphate		29,887	 Lapanto Glory	20/3</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
